{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 9, :comments ["<b>Is it but a small thing for you, etc.</b> It does not say 'for you' but rather 'from you' — for he is speaking of the rebellion and the trespass that goes forth from you. And is such a rebellion a small and minor thing — that a person to whom some appointment is given should rebel over the fact that they did not give him an appointment greater than this? And some say that he is speaking toward the minority, for the Levites are the fewest of all the tribes: 'For HaShem has set you apart' etc., meaning for the service of the Ark which consumes among you, 'and you seek the priesthood as well' — and you will endanger yourselves even more, for whoever draws nearer to the Ark of the Covenant of HaShem is in greater danger. 'And what is Aaron' — for he was always the most humble and did not consider himself as anything at all; therefore he endures, even though he is closer to HaShem more than all, as they said (Sanhedrin 14a): 'Be receiving and enduring.' But anyone who is not in the measure of humility does not endure if he comes before HaShem with an arrogant heart."], :book :numbers, :voice :kli-yakar, :lang :en, :chapter 16, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:41:32.464665301Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}